  "cites": "the unsupported MODIFY replaced by DENY and recorded correctly in the audit log, and also emitted on the trace as an acs.decision.failure of class malformed_response. The release/0.1.4 text rules these cases out as decision failures: the outcome is defined, so counting it as a failure inflates the failure count and, under the counting rule, stops a reader from counting a decision that was in fact applied as written. Issue 264 rejected the same reuse for that reason.",
